{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Investigation closes this as not-a-bug. The plan-review G6 block was correct: production overlap traffic flows only through judge_batch (wire.py -> judge() -> judge_batch, judge.py:284-285); judge_one is test-only and its in-code 'volume site' comment is stale. Usage-log evidence: every 48000-token failure (out=48000, req=3 = 3 attempts x 16k default cap) is timestamped at or before 2026-08-10T17:39 — checkouts running pre-7fa8102477 code; all failures after the checkout updated (2026-08-11T18:07+) are bounded exactly as the fix intends: out=1024, req=1, ~$0.02 each, degrading to the designed advisory abstain. The 08-08 fix works; the observed storms were stale worktrees. Residual note (non-blocking): a batch whose verdict legitimately exceeds 1024 output tokens abstains — an overlap-recall loss worth revisiting only if drain-abstain rates grow."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786471820036558001,"uuid":"d4744704-20d0-42ea-b559-fc69487e8462"}